# The highest mobile build number recorded as consumed by a store upload.
#
# The reservation job allocates above this committed floor and every recorded
# reservation/published build. github.run_number is a minimum, not the final
# allocation order: queued deliveries may start out of order.
#
# Raise this mark after an upload is accepted or its number is known to be
# consumed, even if later publication fails. Do not lower it or reclaim a
# reserved number after an uncertain upload. Non-contiguous values are valid.
# The durable draft reservation protects the number before upload; this file
# is the reviewed, committed record maintained afterward.
#
# The Mobile release summary names the required follow-up value.
# scripts/check-mobile-build-mark.py compares this mark with the newest
# published mobile asset: lint warns if it lags, and the next mobile release
# refuses to proceed until the record is updated. Keep this independent record
# because a store may accept an upload whose later publication never finishes.
# See docs/mobile-release-process.md for reservation and recovery details.
47
